[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-39428"] :question/problem "Let $u$ and $v$ be vectors such that $‖v‖=5$ and $‖2u+3v‖=17.$  If $u$ is orthogonal to $v$, find $‖u‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ is orthogonal to $v,$ we also have that $2u$ is orthogonal to $3v.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2u+3v{‖}^{2} & =‖2u{‖}^{2}+‖3v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2u+3v{‖}^{2} & =(2‖u‖)^{2}+(3‖v‖)^{2} \\\\ ‖2u+3v{‖}^{2} & =4‖u{‖}^{2}+9‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ (17)^{2} & =4‖u{‖}^{2}+9(5)^{2} \\\\ 289 & =4‖u{‖}^{2}+9\\cdot 25 \\\\ 289 & =4‖u{‖}^{2}+225 \\\\ 64 & =4‖u{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖u{‖}^{2} & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $‖u‖=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-40898/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "6e7d5d15-c297-580d-91ce-fbaeee2a21de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40898/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "7ade5330-5789-5e7d-8e71-9107541d6ec1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40898/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "59063544-b2b6-5e88-a659-c60c70adac73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40898/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "b4c1c52b-a788-53b7-a2a8-6d40a7a2a774" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40898/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "381d9aa7-b698-568f-be67-e9d0e99fe2fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40898/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f480a6d-e13d-5e5b-b53b-33068efcf578" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40898/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer-field/choices ["q-40898/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-40898/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-40898/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-40898/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-40898/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40898" :question/id #uuid "a4b83d81-ba31-544f-aa9b-33ae4c0375b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-40898" :question/problem "Given that $‖6u+v‖=11$ and $‖v‖=2$, find the smallest possible value of $‖u‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖6u+v‖ & \\le ‖6u‖+‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖6u+v‖ & \\le 6‖u‖+‖v‖ \\\\ 11 & \\le 6‖u‖+2 \\\\ 9 & \\le 6‖u‖ \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & \\le ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖u‖$ is $\\frac{3}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-40898/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ae3aec8-4d20-5467-9ced-2a9c1bda3afd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40898"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-40197"] :question/problem "Given that $‖4u+v‖=22$ and $‖v‖=2$, find the smallest possible value of $‖u‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖4u+v‖ & \\le ‖4u‖+‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖4u+v‖ & \\le 4‖u‖+‖v‖ \\\\ 22 & \\le 4‖u‖+2 \\\\ 20 & \\le 4‖u‖ \\\\ 5 & \\le ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖u‖$ is $5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-40901/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "d072ad69-93e9-52a1-afc8-d0a5704d03d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40901/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "bca72d18-fecb-5744-bd39-e1d5b49cea90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40901/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "6fee3d5c-3d75-5da1-ba0c-96e138e1d310" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40901/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "c2d92642-32c8-56d0-b40f-33ee82fd5531" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40901/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "de3edb5a-d179-5629-89b8-495b8b6708b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40901/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "116100a7-46f9-560c-b49c-389696618870" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40901/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-40901/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-40901/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-40901/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-40901/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-40901/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40901" :question/id #uuid "b086fe32-6449-5a47-a5ac-e33d2ec31ab6" :question/math-academy-id "q-40901" :question/problem "Given that $‖9u+v‖=23$ and $‖v‖=5$, find the smallest possible value of $‖u‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖9u+v‖ & \\le ‖9u‖+‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖9u+v‖ & \\le 9‖u‖+‖v‖ \\\\ 23 & \\le 9‖u‖+5 \\\\ 18 & \\le 9‖u‖ \\\\ 2 & \\le ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖u‖$ is $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-40901/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ae3aec8-4d20-5467-9ced-2a9c1bda3afd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40901"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74193/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "09c3a527-8da8-5642-9de9-1b9667b694f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74193/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "09cb2125-ab2e-50a7-b8fc-dd863601f451" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74193/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "3aa45136-9e3d-58c6-93eb-16148c84a764" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74193/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "cf41f401-e0dd-5e32-bdaa-9fc27ac52864" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74193/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "7c6ea1f7-4bda-57b0-8037-cf6086307d85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74193/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4e7400e-0173-5326-a9d8-237cca1079a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74193/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-74193/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-74193/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-74193/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-74193/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-74193/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74193" :question/id #uuid "ac7d1f8c-831e-5e15-b329-401bcc807fb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-74193" :question/problem "Let the vectors $v$ and $w$ be orthogonal. \nIf $|u\\cdot v{|}^{2}+2‖v+w{‖}^{2}=158$ and $‖u‖=‖w‖=5$, then what is the minimum possible value of $‖v‖?$" :question/worked-solution "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}158 & ={|u\\cdot v|}^{2}+2‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & \\le {‖u{‖}^{2}\\cdot ‖v‖}^{2}+2‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & ={5}^{2}\\cdot ‖v{‖}^{2}+2‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & =25‖v{‖}^{2}+2‖v+w{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $v⊥w$, using the Pythagorean theorem, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25‖v{‖}^{2}+2‖v+w{‖}^{2} & =25‖v{‖}^{2}+2(‖v{‖}^{2}+‖w{‖}^{2}) \\\\  & =25‖v{‖}^{2}+2(‖v{‖}^{2}+{5}^{2}) \\\\  & =27‖v{‖}^{2}+50.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two steps above, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}158 & \\le 27‖v‖+50 \\\\ 108 & \\le 27‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 4 & \\le ‖v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $4\\le ‖v{‖}^{2}$ implies that $2\\le ‖v‖.$ Notice that we disregard the negative solutions since the norm can't be negative.\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible value of $‖v‖$ is $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-74193/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2391612a-ee27-5cb2-a194-9b51e6fec1e1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74193"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-40242/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "67e6cc85-4bae-5922-8fb1-262742215a08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40242/selection/5d769efb488a157172b1baa2e9333e8a40ac36c26dea965b52833adef9937f85" :answer/id #uuid "dae480ff-090f-5697-897d-db490c2677b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40242/selection/18eb49ac0d68df1d2f88dde00f678c51227d5479a878308d1c5c70b2471052a2" :answer/id #uuid "f0b35cbf-5529-51a5-bcc1-557a65d58c3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40242/selection/7bd4f74b59bb91fc795413364e0fd5ff6cdead027bd50fe690d4710a6510cef4" :answer/id #uuid "657f1701-472e-5f66-9fb0-790a0ebddd04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{3}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40242/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "b9cabd05-1c3a-515c-8980-dba9fb8a594b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40242/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "777f9c3f-2deb-540b-a837-731ef9a1e092" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40242/selection/7bd4f74b59bb91fc795413364e0fd5ff6cdead027bd50fe690d4710a6510cef4" :answer-field/choices ["q-40242/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-40242/selection/5d769efb488a157172b1baa2e9333e8a40ac36c26dea965b52833adef9937f85" "q-40242/selection/18eb49ac0d68df1d2f88dde00f678c51227d5479a878308d1c5c70b2471052a2" "q-40242/selection/7bd4f74b59bb91fc795413364e0fd5ff6cdead027bd50fe690d4710a6510cef4" "q-40242/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40242" :question/id #uuid "cb63f147-46bc-5152-9034-eaf5b3486fb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-40242" :question/problem "If $|u\\cdot v|+‖u+v‖=12\\sqrt{3}$ and $‖v‖=2\\sqrt{3}$, then what is the smallest possible value of $‖u‖?$" :question/worked-solution "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12\\sqrt{3} & =|u\\cdot v|+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & =‖u‖\\cdot (2\\sqrt{3})+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}‖u‖+‖u+v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using the triangle inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3}‖u‖+‖u+v‖ & \\le 2\\sqrt{3}‖u‖+(‖u‖+‖v‖) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}‖u‖+(‖u‖+2\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =(2\\sqrt{3}+1)‖u‖+2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two inequalities, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12\\sqrt{3} & \\le (2\\sqrt{3}+1)‖u‖+2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 10\\sqrt{3} & \\le (2\\sqrt{3}+1)‖u‖ \\\\ \\frac{10\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{3}+1} & \\le ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖u‖$ is $\\frac{10\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{3}+1}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-40242/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2391612a-ee27-5cb2-a194-9b51e6fec1e1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40242"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140462/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a51