:question/problem "Let the vectors $v$ and $w$ be orthogonal. \nIf $|u\\cdot v{|}^{2}+3‖v+w{‖}^{2}=204$ and $‖u‖=4$ and $‖w‖=7$, then what is the minimum possible value of $‖v‖?$" :question/worked-solution "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}204 & =|u\\cdot v{|}^{2}+3‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & \\le {‖u{‖}^{2}\\cdot ‖v‖}^{2}+3‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}\\cdot ‖v{‖}^{2}+3‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & =16‖v{‖}^{2}+3‖v+w{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $v⊥w$, using the Pythagorean theorem, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16‖v{‖}^{2}+3‖v+w{‖}^{2} & =16‖v{‖}^{2}+3(‖v{‖}^{2}+‖w{‖}^{2}) \\\\  & =16‖v{‖}^{2}+3(‖v{‖}^{2}+{7}^{2}) \\\\  & =19‖v{‖}^{2}+147.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two steps above, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}204 & \\le 19‖v‖+147 \\\\ 57 & \\le 19‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 3 & \\le ‖v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $3\\le ‖v{‖}^{2}$ implies that $\\sqrt{3}\\le ‖v‖.$ Notice that we disregard the negative solutions since the norm can't be negative.\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible value of $‖v‖$ is $\\sqrt{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-140462/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2391612a-ee27-5cb2-a194-9b51e6fec1e1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140462"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
